    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39078" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιγουν-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>part above the knee, great muscle of the thigh</i>, taken
			as a sign of strength and vigour, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεν . .
				μεγάλην ἐπιγουνίδα θεῖτο</span> he would grow a stout
				<i>thigh-muscle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.225
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἵην ἐπιγουνίδα φαίνει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.74
				</span></i>
			,cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				26.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.24
			</span></i>; prob. in this sense in <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.875
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιγονατίς</span>
			, <i>knee-pan</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				70
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Gym.</u>
				35
			</span></i>; <i>knee</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				254
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				614
			</span></i>.</div>
